      Q("There are two blessings in which many people are cheated: health and free time. || Ikki ne’mat borki, ko‘p odamlar ularda aldanib qoladilar: sog‘liq va bo‘sh vaqt.", "Bukhari 6412"),
      L("How life is wasted today || Bugun umr qanday isrof bo‘lmoqda", [
        "Children who should be learning wander the streets, pick up smoking and bad words, and damage things that belong to others. || Ilm olishi kerak bo‘lgan bolalar ko‘chada sang‘ib, chekish va so‘kinishga o‘rganmoqda, odamlarning narsalariga zarar yetkazmoqda.",
        "Grown men sit on street corners in backbiting, cards and board games, wasting the years Allah gave them. || Kattalar ko‘cha burchagida g‘iybat, karta va nard bilan Alloh bergan yillarini zoye qilmoqda.",
        "Some lie in front of the television all day and send others out to earn. || Ba’zilar kun bo‘yi televizor oldida yotib, boshqalarni pul topishga jo‘natadi.",
        "Today we can add endless scrolling and games that eat hours without our noticing. || Bugun bunga cheksiz telefon titkilash va soatlarni sezdirmay yeb qo‘yadigan o‘yinlarni ham qo‘shish mumkin.",
      ]),
      { type: "compare", title: "An hour after school || Maktabdan keyingi bir soat", left: "Wasted || Isrof", right: "Well spent || Unumli", rows: [
        ["Scrolling videos without knowing why || Nima uchunligini bilmay video titkilash", "Reading, revising or learning a sūrah || O‘qish, takrorlash yoki sura yodlash"],
        ["Wandering outside with nothing to do || Ishsiz ko‘chada sang‘ish", "Playing sport or helping at home || Sport yoki uyda yordam"],
        ["Talking about other people || Boshqalar haqida gapirish", "Visiting a grandparent or a sick neighbour || Bobo-buvi yoki bemor qo‘shnini ziyorat qilish"],
      ] },
      { type: "reflect", think: ["If I counted my screen time this week, what else could those hours have been? || Bu hafta ekran vaqtimni hisoblasam, o‘sha soatlar yana nima bo‘lishi mumkin edi?", "What is one thing I keep saying I have no time for? || Doim “vaqtim yo‘q” deydigan bitta ishim nima?"],
        home: ["Make a family “time budget” for one week: sleep, school or work, prayer, family, learning, rest and play. See where the hours really go. || Bir hafta uchun oilaviy “vaqt byudjeti” tuzing: uyqu, maktab yoki ish, namoz, oila, o‘qish, dam olish va o‘yin. Soatlar aslida qayerga ketayotganini ko‘ring."] },
      L("Key takeaways || Asosiy xulosalar", [
        "Life is our most precious blessing, and we will be asked how we spent it. || Umr — eng aziz ne’mat, uni qanday o‘tkazganimiz so‘raladi.",
        "Health and free time are blessings many people are cheated of. || Sog‘liq va bo‘sh vaqt — ko‘pchilik aldanib qoladigan ne’matlar.",
        "Spend time on faith, good deeds, learning and helping others. || Vaqtni iymon, solih amal, ilm va boshqalarga yordamga sarflang.",
      ]),
    ],
    quiz: [
      { q: "What is the first thing in the ḥadīth of the four questions? || To‘rt savol hadisida birinchi so‘raladigan narsa nima?", options: ["Your clothes || Kiyimingiz", "Your life and how you spent it || Umringiz va uni nimada o‘tkazganingiz", "Your house || Uyingiz", "Your friends || Do‘stlaringiz"], answer: 1, why: "Then knowledge, wealth and the body. || Keyin ilm, mol va jism.", src: "Tirmidhi 2417" },
      { q: "Which two blessings are many people cheated of? || Ko‘p odamlar qaysi ikki ne’matda aldanib qoladi?", options: ["Gold and silver || Tilla va kumush", "Health and free time || Sog‘liq va bo‘sh vaqt", "Food and drink || Taom va ichimlik", "Cars and houses || Mashina va uylar"], answer: 1, why: "They do not use them until they lose them. || Ularni yo‘qotgunlaricha qadriga yetmaydilar.", src: "Bukhari 6412" },
      { q: "According to Sūrat al-ʿAṣr, who is NOT in loss? || Asr surasiga ko‘ra kim ziyonda EMAS?", options: ["The rich || Boylar", "Those who believe, do good, and urge truth and patience || Iymon keltirgan, solih amal qilgan, haq va sabrni tavsiya qilganlar", "The famous || Mashhurlar", "Everyone || Hamma"], answer: 1, why: "Everyone else is in loss. || Qolganlar ziyonda.", src: "Quran 103:1–3" },
      { q: "Spending your life on useless things is… || Umrni behuda narsalarga sarflash…", options: ["…a kind of isrof || …isrofning bir turi", "…fine if you are young || …yosh bo‘lsang mayli", "…a sunnah || …sunnat", "…rewarded || …savobli"], answer: 0, why: "We will answer for every moment. || Har lahzasi uchun javob beramiz.", src: B("Infoq-xarajatdagi isrof") },
      { q: "What will we be asked about our knowledge? || Ilmimiz haqida nima so‘raladi?", options: ["How long it took || Qancha vaqt olgani", "What we did with it || U bilan nima qilganimiz", "Who taught us || Kim o‘rgatgani", "Nothing || Hech narsa"], answer: 1, why: "Knowledge should benefit people. || Ilm odamlarga foyda berishi kerak.", src: "Tirmidhi 2417" },
      { q: "What will we be asked about our body? || Jismimiz haqida nima so‘raladi?", options: ["What we wore it out in || Uni nimada qaritganimiz", "Its height || Bo‘yi", "Its colour || Rangi", "Its name || Ismi"], answer: 0, why: "The body is a trust to use well. || Jism — yaxshi ishlatiladigan omonat.", src: "Tirmidhi 2417" },
      { q: "Which is an example of wasting life given in the book? || Kitobda umrni isrof qilishga qanday misol keltirilgan?", options: ["Reading the Quran || Qur’on o‘qish", "Sitting in backbiting and card games || G‘iybat va karta o‘yini bilan o‘tirish", "Helping parents || Ota-onaga yordam", "Going to school || Maktabga borish"], answer: 1, why: "The book mentions both children and elders wasting their years. || Kitobda bolalar ham, kattalar ham yillarini zoye qilishi aytilgan.", src: B("Turli maishiy isroflar") },
      { q: "Which is the best use of an hour after school? || Maktabdan keyingi bir soatni o‘tkazishning eng yaxshisi qaysi?", options: ["Scrolling videos || Video titkilash", "Wandering the streets || Ko‘chada sang‘ish", "Learning, sport, or helping someone || O‘qish, sport yoki birovga yordam", "Talking about people || Odamlar haqida gapirish"], answer: 2, why: "Time used for good is never wasted. || Yaxshilikka sarflangan vaqt hech zoye bo‘lmaydi.", src: "Quran 103:1–3" },
      { q: "Why is life called the most precious blessing? || Nega umr eng aziz ne’mat deyiladi?", options: ["Because it can be bought again || Chunki uni qayta sotib olish mumkin", "Because a moment that passes never comes back || Chunki o‘tgan lahza hech qaytmaydi", "Because it is long || Chunki u uzun", "It is not precious || U qadrli emas"], answer: 1, why: "Money can be earned again; time cannot. || Pulni qayta topish mumkin, vaqtni emas.", src: B("Turli maishiy isroflar") },
      { q: "A good way to see where a family’s time goes is… || Oila vaqti qayerga ketayotganini ko‘rishning yaxshi yo‘li…", options: ["…a weekly time budget || …haftalik vaqt byudjeti", "…buying a new TV || …yangi televizor olish", "…sleeping more || …ko‘proq uxlash", "…ignoring it || …e’tibor bermaslik"], answer: 0, why: "What gets counted gets cared for. || Hisoblangan narsa asraladi.", src: B("Turli maishiy isroflar") },
    ],
  },

  {
    id: "childhood-without-waste", group: "Kinds of isrof || Isrofning turlari",
    title: "A childhood without waste || Isrofsiz bolalik",
    summary: "Childhood is the best time to learn. How parents raise children who value food, things and time, and how children can guard their own years. || Bolalik — o‘rganishning eng yaxshi vaqti. Ota-onalar ne’mat, narsa va vaqtni qadrlaydigan farzandni qanday tarbiyalaydi va bolalar o‘z yillarini qanday asraydi.",
    sources: [B("Isrofning sabablari"), B("Turli maishiy isroflar"), "Quran 66:6", "Bukhari 893", "Muslim 2033"],
    blocks: [
      P("A child who grows up in waste thinks waste is normal. The book teaches that it is the duty of adults to raise children far from isrof and close to thrift. Habits planted in childhood stay for life, and so do the years spent well or badly. || Isrofda o‘sgan bola isrofni oddiy hol deb biladi. Kitobda bolalarni isrofdan uzoq va tejamkorlikka yaqin qilib tarbiyalash kattalarning vazifasi ekani aytilgan. Bolalikda ekilgan odat umrbod qoladi, yaxshi yoki yomon o‘tgan yillar ham shunday."),
      Q("O you who believe, protect yourselves and your families from a Fire. || Ey iymon keltirganlar! O‘zingizni va ahli oilangizni do‘zaxdan saqlang.", "Quran 66:6"),
      L("For parents: what the book advises || Ota-onalar uchun: kitob maslahatlari", [
        "Teach good character and keep children away from bad company. || Yaxshi axloqni o‘rgating va bolani yomon do‘stlardan saqlang.",
        "Do not get them used to chasing passing pleasures and showy things, so they do not spend their lives running after them when they grow up. || Ularni o‘tkinchi lazzat va zebu ziynatga o‘rgatmang, toki katta bo‘lganda umrini ularning ortidan quvib o‘tkazmasin.",
        "The first bad habit to watch for is greed for food. Teach the manners of eating, and sometimes let them eat plain bread, so they do not think every bite needs something added. || Bolada birinchi kuzatiladigan yomon odat — taomga o‘chlik. Ovqatlanish odobini o‘rgating, ba’zan faqat non yeyishga ham odatlantiring, toki har luqmaga biror narsa qo‘shish shart, deb o‘ylamasin.",
        "Explain that eating in a rush without noticing when you are full is how animals eat, not people of adab. || Qorni to‘yganini sezmay, apil-tapil yeyish hayvonlarning ishi, odobli insonning ishi emasligini tushuntiring.",
        "Be the example. Children copy what they see far more than what they hear. || O‘rnak bo‘ling. Bolalar eshitganidan ko‘ra ko‘rganiga ko‘proq ergashadi.",
      ]),
      L("For children: guarding your own years || Bolalar uchun: o‘z yillaringizni asrang", [
        "Your childhood is when your mind learns fastest. Every sūrah, skill and good habit you learn now stays with you. || Bolalikda aql eng tez o‘rganadi. Hozir o‘rgangan har bir sura, mahorat va yaxshi odat siz bilan qoladi.",
        "Do not waste it wandering, swearing, smoking or breaking other people’s things, as the book warns. || Kitob ogohlantirganidek, uni ko‘chada sang‘ish, so‘kinish, chekish yoki boshqalarning narsasini buzish bilan zoye qilmang.",
        "Look after your things: clothes, books, toys and devices. A broken toy that could be fixed is a small waste; a habit of breaking is a big one. || Narsalaringizni asrang: kiyim, kitob, o‘yinchoq va qurilmalar. Tuzatsa bo‘ladigan buzuq o‘yinchoq — kichik isrof, buzish odati — katta isrof.",
        "Finish your plate, turn off the lights, and close the tap. Small habits make a person who does not waste. || Likopchangizni tugating, chiroqni o‘chiring, jo‘mrakni yoping. Kichik odatlar isrof qilmaydigan insonni yasaydi.",
      ]),
      { type: "story", id: "isrof-boy-bread", kind: "A story to learn from", title: "The piece of bread || Bir burda non",
        scene: "A story the book’s teaching brings to mind: a family meal, and a crust that fell to the floor. || Kitob ta’limoti eslatadigan voqea: oilaviy dasturxon va yerga tushgan bir burda non.",
        story: [
          "A boy dropped a piece of bread while eating and left it on the floor. His grandfather picked it up, wiped it, and ate it. || Bola ovqatlanayotib bir burda nonni yerga tushirib, o‘sha yerda qoldirdi. Bobosi uni olib, tozalab, yedi.",
          "“Why did you eat that, Grandad?” asked the boy. || “Nega uni yedingiz, bobo?” deb so‘radi bola.",
          "“The Prophet ﷺ told us: if a morsel falls, remove what is on it and eat it, and do not leave it for Shayṭān. You do not know where the blessing in your food is.” || “Payg‘ambarimiz ﷺ: luqma tushsa, undagi noloyiq narsani ketkazib yesin, uni shaytonga qoldirmasin, dedilar. Taomingning qayerida baraka borligini bilmaysan.”",
          "The next day, the boy was the first to pick up a fallen crumb. || Ertasi kuni yerga tushgan uvoqni birinchi bo‘lib bola oldi.",
        ],
        lesson: "Children learn respect for blessings from what adults do, not only from what they say. || Bolalar ne’matni hurmat qilishni kattalarning gapidan emas, ishidan o‘rganadi.",
        src: "Muslim 2033",
        check: { q: "What did the Prophet ﷺ say to do with a fallen morsel? || Payg‘ambar ﷺ yerga tushgan luqmani nima qilishni aytdilar?", options: ["Throw it away || Tashlab yuborish", "Clean it and eat it, not leave it for Shayṭān || Tozalab yeyish, shaytonga qoldirmaslik", "Give it to a cat || Mushukka berish", "Leave it there || O‘sha yerda qoldirish"], answer: 1, why: "You do not know where the blessing is. || Baraka qayerda ekanini bilmaysiz." } },
      { type: "reflect", think: ["What habits about food, money and time am I passing on to my children without words? || Ovqat, pul va vaqt haqida farzandlarimga so‘zsiz qanday odatlarni o‘tkazyapman?", "Children: what is one thing I can learn this year that I will be glad of when I am grown up? || Bolalar: katta bo‘lganimda xursand bo‘ladigan, bu yil o‘rgana oladigan bitta narsam nima?"],
        home: ["Give each child a small “keeper” job: switching off lights, checking taps, or saving leftovers in the fridge. Praise them when they do it. || Har bir bolaga kichik “qo‘riqchi” vazifasini bering: chiroqlarni o‘chirish, jo‘mraklarni tekshirish yoki ortgan ovqatni muzlatgichga solish. Bajarganda maqtang."] },
      L("Key takeaways || Asosiy xulosalar", [
        "Raising children away from waste is the duty of the adults. || Bolalarni isrofdan uzoq tarbiyalash kattalarning vazifasi.",
        "Watch for greed for food first, and teach the manners of eating. || Avvalo taomga o‘chlikni kuzating va ovqatlanish odobini o‘rgating.",
        "Childhood is the best time to learn; do not waste it. || Bolalik — o‘rganishning eng yaxshi vaqti; uni isrof qilmang.",
      ]),
    ],
    quiz: [
      { q: "Whose duty is it to raise children far from waste? || Bolalarni isrofdan uzoq tarbiyalash kimning vazifasi?", options: ["The children’s alone || Faqat bolalarning", "The adults’ || Kattalarning", "The shopkeepers’ || Do‘kondorlarning", "No one’s || Hech kimning"], answer: 1, why: "“Protect yourselves and your families” (66:6). || “O‘zingizni va ahli oilangizni saqlang” (66:6).", src: "Quran 66:6" },
      { q: "What is the first bad habit to watch for in a child, according to the book? || Kitobga ko‘ra bolada birinchi kuzatiladigan yomon odat qaysi?", options: ["Greed for food || Taomga o‘chlik", "Reading too much || Ko‘p o‘qish", "Sleeping early || Erta uxlash", "Being quiet || Jim bo‘lish"], answer: 0, why: "So teach the manners of eating. || Shuning uchun ovqatlanish odobini o‘rgating.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "Why does the book suggest sometimes letting children eat plain bread? || Kitob nega bolani ba’zan faqat non yeyishga odatlantirishni maslahat beradi?", options: ["To punish them || Jazolash uchun", "So they do not think every bite needs something added || Har luqmaga biror narsa qo‘shish shart, deb o‘ylamasligi uchun", "Because bread is cheap || Non arzon bo‘lgani uchun", "To make them sad || Xafa qilish uchun"], answer: 1, why: "It teaches contentment. || Bu qanoatni o‘rgatadi.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "What do children copy most? || Bolalar ko‘proq nimaga ergashadi?", options: ["What adults do || Kattalarning ishiga", "Only what they hear || Faqat eshitganiga", "Nothing || Hech narsaga", "Only cartoons || Faqat multfilmlarga"], answer: 0, why: "Example teaches more than words. || O‘rnak so‘zdan ko‘ra ko‘proq o‘rgatadi.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "What should be done with a morsel that falls? || Yerga tushgan luqmani nima qilish kerak?", options: ["Leave it || Qoldirish", "Clean it and eat it || Tozalab yeyish", "Step on it || Bosib o‘tish", "Throw it in the bin || Axlatga tashlash"], answer: 1, why: "Do not leave it for Shayṭān. || Uni shaytonga qoldirmang.", src: "Muslim 2033" },
      { q: "Why should parents not get children used to showy things? || Nega ota-onalar bolani zebu ziynatga o‘rgatmasligi kerak?", options: ["So they do not spend their lives chasing them later || Keyin umrini ularning ortidan quvib o‘tkazmasligi uchun", "Because they are too cheap || Chunki ular juda arzon", "There is no reason || Hech sababi yo‘q", "So they never smile || Hech kulmasligi uchun"], answer: 0, why: "Childhood habits last a lifetime. || Bolalik odatlari umrbod qoladi.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "Which is a way children waste their childhood, according to the book? || Kitobga ko‘ra bolalar bolaligini qanday isrof qiladi?", options: ["Learning sūrahs || Sura yodlash", "Wandering the streets, swearing and breaking things || Ko‘chada sang‘ish, so‘kinish va narsalarni buzish", "Helping at home || Uyda yordam berish", "Going to school || Maktabga borish"], answer: 1, why: "Instead of learning. || Ilm olish o‘rniga.", src: B("Turli maishiy isroflar") },
      { q: "Eating in a rush without noticing you are full is… || To‘yganini sezmay apil-tapil yeyish…", options: ["…good manners || …yaxshi odob", "…not the way of people of adab || …odobli insonning ishi emas", "…a sunnah || …sunnat", "…healthy || …foydali"], answer: 1, why: "The book calls it the way animals eat. || Kitob buni hayvonlarning ishi deydi.", src: B("Isrofning sabablari") },
      { q: "Why is childhood called the best time to learn? || Nega bolalik o‘rganishning eng yaxshi vaqti deyiladi?", options: ["Because the mind learns fastest then || Chunki aql o‘shanda eng tez o‘rganadi", "Because there is no school || Chunki maktab yo‘q", "It is not || Unday emas", "Because children are rich || Chunki bolalar boy"], answer: 0, why: "What you learn young stays with you. || Yoshlikda o‘rganilgan narsa qoladi.", src: B("Turli maishiy isroflar") },
      { q: "Which is a good “keeper” job for a child at home? || Uyda bola uchun yaxshi “qo‘riqchi” vazifasi qaysi?", options: ["Leaving lights on || Chiroqni yoniq qoldirish", "Switching off lights and checking taps || Chiroqlarni o‘chirish va jo‘mraklarni tekshirish", "Throwing away leftovers || Ortgan ovqatni tashlash", "Breaking old toys || Eski o‘yinchoqlarni sindirish"], answer: 1, why: "Small habits build a person who does not waste. || Kichik odatlar isrofsiz insonni yasaydi.", src: B("Turli maishiy isroflar") },
    ],
  },

  {
    id: "water", group: "Kinds of isrof || Isrofning turlari",
    title: "Water, the source of life || Suv — hayot manbai",
    summary: "Allah made every living thing from water. The Prophet ﷺ made wuḍūʾ with one mudd. How we waste water today and how to save it. || Alloh har bir tirik narsani suvdan yaratdi. Payg‘ambar ﷺ bir mudd suv bilan tahorat qilardilar. Bugun suvni qanday isrof qilyapmiz va uni qanday tejash mumkin.",
    sources: [B("Suvning isrofi haqida"), B("Isrof qilishdan to‘xtang!"), "Quran 21:30", "Quran 24:45", "Bukhari 201", "Muslim 325", "Abu Dawud 4776"],
    blocks: [
      P("Water is one of Allah’s greatest gifts. Without it there is no life: no people, no animals, no plants, no bread. Growing one kilogram of wheat takes about one and a half thousand litres of water. Our early scholars cared about water so much that they wrote chapters in fiqh on “not wasting water, even when taking it from the sea”. || Suv Allohning eng ulug‘ ne’matlaridan. Usiz hayot yo‘q: na odam, na hayvon, na o‘simlik, na non. Bir kilogramm bug‘doy yetishtirish uchun bir yarim ming litrga yaqin suv kerak. Ulamolarimiz suvga shunchalik e’tibor berganlarki, fiqh kitoblarida “Dengizdan olganda ham suvni isrof qilmaslik haqida” degan boblar ochganlar."),
      Q("And We made from water every living thing. || Va suvdan har bir tirik narsani (paydo) qilganmiz.", "Quran 21:30"),
      L("How the Prophet ﷺ used water || Payg‘ambar ﷺ suvni qanday ishlatgan", [
        "He made wuḍūʾ with one mudd (about two handfuls, roughly two-thirds of a litre) and ghusl with one ṣāʿ up to five mudd (Bukhari 201; Muslim 325). || U zot bir mudd (taxminan ikki hovuch, uchdan ikki litrga yaqin) suv bilan tahorat, bir so‘dan besh muddgacha suv bilan g‘usl qilardilar (Buxoriy 201; Muslim 325).",
        "Craftsmen of old made wuḍūʾ jugs and ghusl vessels that held exactly the amount the jurists set, and people kept to it. || Qadimgi ustalar tahorat va g‘usl idishlarini aynan fuqaholar belgilagan miqdor sig‘adigan qilib yasaganlar, odamlar bunga amal qilishgan.",
        "He warned Saʿd that waste in wuḍūʾ is waste “even at a flowing river”. || U zot Sa’dni tahoratdagi isrof “hatto oqib turgan daryoda bo‘lsang ham” isrof ekanidan ogohlantirganlar.",
        "Good guidance, a good appearance and moderation are a part of prophethood (Abu Dawud 4776). || Solih hidoyat, go‘zal ko‘rinish va iqtisodli bo‘lish nubuvvatning bir juzidir (Abu Dovud 4776).",
      ]),
      { type: "story", id: "isrof-masjid-tap", kind: "From the lives of the scholars", title: "The tap that kept running || Oqib turaverdi",
        scene: "A polite visitor came to the Shaykh with a worry about the wuḍūʾ rooms of the masjids. || Bir odobli inson Shayxning huzuriga masjid tahoratxonalari haqidagi tashvishi bilan keldi.",
        story: [
          "“Even where signs say ‘Please do not waste water’, people sit right under them and let it pour,” he said. “May I gently tell a brother when I see it?” “Yes,” said the Shaykh, “politely and kindly.” || “Hatto ‘Iltimos, suvni isrof qilmang’ degan yozuv bor joyda ham odamlar tagida o‘tirib, suvni oqizib yuborishadi”, dedi u. “Ko‘rsam, birodarga muloyimlik bilan aytsam bo‘ladimi?” Shayx: “Bo‘ladi, odob bilan, sekinlik bilan”, dedilar.",
          "Later, one of the scholars told what he had seen: a man opened the tap all the way, washed his face and arms, then took off his shoe and sock, washed one foot, dried it, put the sock and shoe back on, and did the same with the other foot, and all the while the water ran. || Keyin olimlardan biri ko‘rganini aytib berdi: bir kishi jo‘mrakni oxirigacha ochib, yuz-qo‘lini yuvdi, so‘ng oyoq kiyimi va paypog‘ini yechib, bir oyog‘ini yuvdi, artdi, paypoq va oyoq kiyimini kiydi, keyin ikkinchi oyog‘ini ham shunday qildi — shu vaqt bo‘yi suv oqib turaverdi.",
          "Someone said kindly, “Brother, the water is being wasted.” The man answered with a sneer: “Have people become so clever?” || Bir kishi muloyimlik bilan: “Birodar, suv isrof bo‘lyapti”, dedi. U esa istehzo bilan: “Odamlar juda aqlli bo‘lib ketishibdimi?” dedi.",
        ],
        lesson: "Careless waste in the very place of worship shows how far we are from the Sunnah. Turning off a tap takes a second; it is a small act of obedience. || Ibodat joyining o‘zida beparvo isrof Sunnatdan qanchalik uzoqlashganimizni ko‘rsatadi. Jo‘mrakni yopish bir soniya oladi; bu kichik itoatdir.",
        src: "Isrof, “Isrof qilishdan to‘xtang!”",
        check: { q: "How did the Shaykh say to advise someone wasting water? || Shayx suvni isrof qilayotganga qanday nasihat qilishni aytdilar?", options: ["Shout at him || Unga baqirish", "Politely and gently || Odob bilan, sekinlik bilan", "Take a photo and post it || Suratga olib, joylash", "Say nothing ever || Hech qachon hech narsa demaslik"], answer: 1, why: "Advice is given with adab. || Nasihat odob bilan qilinadi." } },
      { type: "compare", title: "Water at home || Uydagi suv", left: "Wasteful || Isrof", right: "Thrifty || Tejamkor", rows: [
        ["Tap open while brushing teeth or between washing each foot || Tish yuvayotganda yoki oyoqlar orasida jo‘mrak ochiq", "Open only when you need the water || Faqat suv kerak bo‘lganda oching"],
